## Summary

**seq209 ORCH ContextDoc REVISION** (CEO live-preview feedback) → intake-confirmed the defect against the code, then sliced + assigned (`7d3f5c5a`, `ed5c9251`, `bb78991c`).

**Defect verified, not trusted**: `render_chat()` emits the same `<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="5">` as the status page → /chat full-reloads every 5s (jump-to-top, loses scroll + open `<details>`). Real UX bug; blocks merge. No challenge.

**Slice issued (lean, per "speed over polish"):**
- **FE (primary, TCK-...-FE-rev1)**: remove the meta-refresh from `/chat` only (keep it on `/`); make reading scroll-stable (simplest non-jumping approach — fragment-poll + scroll restore, or pinned-bottom append, or drop-refresh + "new messages" affordance); inline stdlib JS, no frameworks/websockets, **no gold-plating**.
- **BE (conditional, TCK-...-BE-rev1)**: minimal `/chat/feed` fragment endpoint *only if FE needs it*, reusing the existing `build_feed`/`_chat_row` escaped path; coordinate so one of them edits the meta-refresh line.
- **Hard architecture constraint I enforced**: XSS-no-regression — inject only server-escaped HTML, keep the single XSS surface in BE; SEC re-checks any new sink.
- **TDD**: route test asserts `/chat` emits no full-page meta-refresh while `/` still does.
- **Keep unchanged**: `/` status page, XSS-safety, headline ladder.

**Status**: the f6fcc4a ApprovalRequest is effectively paused for this pre-merge revision. Once FE/BE land the fix on `feat/chatview-be`, I fast-review and emit the new sha to ORCH for CEO re-preview, then SEC/QA/PLAT re-pin. Nothing further to act on this wake.
